# Standards: Frontend (node-react-prisma stack)
> Extends `core/standards/core.mdc`. Read core first.
> Stack: React 18 · TypeScript 5 · shadcn/ui · Tailwind CSS 3 · React Router 6 · Axios · Playwright

---

## 1. Project Structure

```
src/frontend/src/
├── components/         # Reusable UI components (no business logic, no direct API calls)
│   ├── common/         # Truly generic: Button, Modal, Alert, Spinner wrappers
│   └── {feature}/      # Feature-scoped: EmployeeCard, ProjectList
├── pages/              # Route-level components — orchestrate, no raw UI logic
├── hooks/              # Custom hooks: useEmployee, useProjectData, useFormValidation
├── services/           # All API calls — never axios directly in components
├── types/              # TypeScript: domain.types.ts, api.types.ts
├── constants/          # ROUTES, STATUS_VALUES, API_BASE_URL
├── assets/             # Images, fonts
├── App.tsx             # Router setup + route definitions
└── index.tsx           # Entry point
```

**Rule:** Components in `components/` never call `services/` directly.
Data flows: `services/` → `pages/` or `hooks/` → `components/` via props.

---

## 1b. shadcn/ui usage

Always import shadcn components from `@/components/ui/`:

```typescript
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"
import { Input } from "@/components/ui/input"
import { Table, TableBody, TableCell, TableHead, TableHeader, TableRow } from "@/components/ui/table"
```

Never install raw Radix UI primitives directly — use the shadcn wrapper.
Never use raw HTML `<button>`, `<input>`, `<table>` — always use the shadcn equivalent.
Use Tailwind utility classes for layout and spacing. Never write custom CSS files.

